{"type":"step-attempt","step":"code-review","sessionId":"0439e2b3-042b-4c1c-9628-95e229fe406b","outcome":{"verdict":"needs-fix","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/runtime-strategy-convergence/review-feedback-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"findings":[{"severity":"high","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/core/port/__tests__/runtime-strategy-ratchet.test.ts","title":"Architecture ratchet REPO_ROOT has off-by-one: scans no files, all assertions pass vacuously","rationale":"The constant uses 5 `..` segments but the comment above says 4 levels up. From `src/core/port/__tests__`, 4 `..` reaches the repo root; the 5th `..` escapes to the parent directory. SRC_DIR and TESTS_DIR therefore don't exist, `collectTsFiles` returns [], and every `expect([]).toHaveLength(0)` passes without scanning a single real file. All 8 ratchet assertions (TC-008, TC-009, TC-010, TC-011, TC-012, TC-031, canDeriveChangedFiles, RealRuntimeStrategy) provide zero protection.","line":117},{"severity":"medium","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/core/port/command-runtime.ts","title":"JobBootstrapCapability JSDoc says managed assertNoDuplicateLiveJob is no-op; implementation calls assertSlugUnoccupied","rationale":"The interface JSDoc documents `- managed: assertNoDuplicateLiveJob is no-op.` but ManagedRuntime.assertNoDuplicateLiveJob (managed.ts:618) delegates to `assertSlugUnoccupied` identically to LocalRuntime. TC-028-managed only verifies happy-path resolution (resolves on fresh dir), not no-op behavior. The stale comment on assertProviderReadiness in managed.ts line 627 (`No-op — mirrors assertNoDuplicateLiveJob convention`) compounds the confusion by incorrectly implying assertNoDuplicateLiveJob is a convention-setter for no-op.","line":50},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/core/runtime/managed.ts","title":"Stale JSDoc references removed concepts: optional chaining in runner.ts and RealRuntimeStrategy","rationale":"Lines 606-608 say 'The optional-chaining call in runner.ts uses `?.`, so if this method were absent the fallback would be used — but RealRuntimeStrategy requires it'. Both references are obsolete: reloadJobState is now required on JobStatePersistenceCapability (no optional chaining in runner.ts), and RealRuntimeStrategy was deleted. Additionally, provider-readiness.ts line 5 says 'required on RealRuntimeStrategy' which is also stale. After fixing the ratchet path bug (Finding 1), TC-009 would flag managed.ts:607 and provider-readiness.ts:5 as violations.","line":607},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"tests/unit/core/command/runner.test.ts","title":"Test fake still typed as RuntimeStrategy & PipelineDepsBuilder instead of RuntimeFacade","rationale":"Lines 94 and 148 use `RuntimeStrategy & PipelineDepsBuilder` as the return/parameter type for the test fake and TestCommand constructor. The acceptance criterion states 'test fake は typed builder/helper で必要 contract を満たす'. The ratchet TC-008 only guards production source (collectProductionFiles excludes __tests__), so this is not caught automatically.","line":94}],"evidence":{"checked":23,"skipped":0,"unverified":2},"observations":[{"severity":"low","file":"src/core/pipeline/runtime-capability-gate.ts","title":"Uses Pick<ChangedFilesCapability, 'canDeriveChangedFiles'> for parameter narrowing","rationale":"The gate parameter type uses `Pick<ChangedFilesCapability, 'canDeriveChangedFiles'>` rather than the full `ChangedFilesCapability` interface. This is outside the ratchet scope (guards `Pick<RuntimeStrategy` not `Pick<ChangedFilesCapability`) and is an acceptable structural narrowing. No action required.","line":71},{"severity":"low","file":"src/core/runtime/__tests__/command-lifecycle-contract.test.ts","title":"TC-028 Managed runtime test comment acknowledges non-no-op behavior","rationale":"The TC-028-managed test comment says 'Both LocalRuntime and ManagedRuntime call assertSlugUnoccupied', correctly describing the implementation but contradicting both the interface JSDoc ('managed: no-op') and the test-cases.md spec ('no-op を検証するテストが含まれている'). Related to Finding 2.","line":148}]},"followUpAttempts":1,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":1}},"startedAt":"2026-09-01T03:41:36.154Z","endedAt":"2026-09-01T03:50:49.588Z","commitOid":"b21983291c3d3c22d74b3871e49c7783a0ff0e38"}
